{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And his heart went numb.</b> He fainted, and his heartbeat and spirit diminished somewhat from what they had been before — as is customary in a faint brought on by the heart's anguish when they mentioned Joseph." "<b>For he did not believe them.</b> Therefore <b>and the spirit of Jacob revived</b> — and his spirit did not depart afterward when he did believe, as would happen in the case of sudden, deadly joy, when the vital spirit rushes outward. For indeed it had withdrawn inward during the prior anguish, when he did not believe."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:47.239761216Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}